WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:04.070
-As a new poll shows majority
support for impeaching

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.172
President Trump,
Republicans are doing everything

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.674
they can to rig
the Senate trial in his favor.

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.943
For more on this it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:14.847
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:17.317
On Friday the House
Judiciary Committee approved

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.151
two articles of impeachment
against Trump,

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:22.588
setting the stage for a vote
of the full House this week.

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:25.425
And as CNN reported,
Trump is aggravated by the fact

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.826
that he's about
to become the third

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.928
President in history
to be impeached.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.864
-We are hearing President Trump
is growing increasingly

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:35.100
aggravated over the likelihood
that he will be impeached.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.837
A Trump campaign adviser
I spoke with earlier today

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.873
told me simply,
"The coverage bugs him."

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:42.275
-Bugs him?

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:45.044
I don't think bugs is ever
the right word for Trump.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.779
He's never just bugged.

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:50.583
He only has two modes --
blind rage or spaced out.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.051
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:55.254
Either screaming like he just
ate a fistful of ghost peppers

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:57.991
or looking straight down
to the table

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:01.761
like an eighth grader
in detention.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.329
Trump's
definitely more than bugged

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.131
by the impeachment coverage.
I mean, look at him.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:08.501
When he gets angry, he looks
like the love child of The Hulk

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.037
and an old bean bag chair
full of farts.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.339
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.174
Also Trump has made it
pretty clear

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:16.542
in his recent
public statements

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.611
that he's more than
just bugged by impeachment,

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:22.481
including a rally last week
and in the Oval Office on Friday

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:23.816
when he claimed the Democrats

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.885
had somehow been trying
to impeach him

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.821
since before he announced that
he was running for President

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.723
back in 2015.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.659
-They can't win on election day.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:36.296
So they're pursuing an illegal,
invalid,

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:40.967
and unconstitutional,
bull[bleep] impeachment.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.802
And then they announced
there was no bias.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:46.972
No, you know what we're doing,
and it's not easy.

00:01:46.972 --> 00:01:51.043
A regular President would have
been under a table, thumb

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:53.579
in the mouth,
saying, "Take me home, Mommy.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.080
This is too tough for me."

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.752
I have to tell you, as bad as
it is, it meant something.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:03.656
When you had serious
high crimes and misdemeanors.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.625
The impeachment is a hoax.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.427
It's a sham.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:10.196
It started a long time ago.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.800
Probably before I came down
the escalator with the future

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.634
First Lady.
-Alright, first of all,

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.103
what's with all the slurring,
man?

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.371
Trump's going to be the first

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.773
President to get pulled over
for a sobriety test

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:24.443
in the middle
of one of his rallies.

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:26.178
Can you say the alphabet
backwards?

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:29.115
"I can't say it forwards."

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:32.351
Second, don't say I came down
the escalator

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:35.187
like you were George Washington
crossing the Delaware.

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:37.890
It wasn't noble or cool.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.826
You rode an escalator
to announce your campaign

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:43.062
for President like you
were at a Macy's

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:46.299
looking for men's underwear.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.533
"I'm running for President.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:53.006
Also, where do you
keep your dumpiest khakis?"

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.074
Third and most important,
you think Democrats

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.809
were secretly plotting
to impeach you

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.746
before you announced that you
were running for President?

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.113
How'd that work?

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:02.748
You think President Obama,
Hillary Clinton and Nancy Pelosi

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.483
were all in a secret room
together saying,

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:06.986
"Okay, you know that famously
dumb game show host?

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.287
You know, the one who spends
most of the time

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:09.388
yelling at Meatloaf?

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:11.024
Well, he's about to ride
an escalator

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.258
down to announce
his campaign.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.060
So here's our plan
to bring him down.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.095
We're going to win the popular
vote by three million votes.

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.430
But then we'll lose
the electoral college

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.565
because, you know,
it's a dumb, antiquated system.

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:20.900
And then we're going to wait
three years

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.035
until he calls
the president of Ukraine

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:26.305
and ask him to dig up
dirt on Joe Biden,

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:29.008
who will announce that
he's running for President.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.943
And also Rudy Giuliani's
going to go on TV

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:32.478
and confess to everything.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.880
That's the plan."

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.447
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:35.447 --> 00:03:37.216
"That is our plan."

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:40.386
Actually, you know,
the last part right

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.021
there is probably
the only thing

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:44.657
they could have predicted
right there.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.460
This is just the world
we live in now.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.296
The president's a deranged,
conspiratorial lunatic

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.131
who's fundamentally untethered
from reality.

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.599
In fact, on Friday, Trump lied

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.001
and claimed
that his poll numbers

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.803
have actually gone up
since impeachment began.

00:03:57.803 --> 00:04:00.873
-My poll numbers as you know
have gone through the roof.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:03.842
The polls have gone
through the roof for Trump.

00:04:03.842 --> 00:04:06.546
Because people, especially
with independent voters,

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:08.147
and especially
in swing states --

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.915
I could show you numbers

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:12.551
that nobody's ever seen numbers
like this before.

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:15.654
[ Laughter ]
-What are you talking about?

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:19.625
"We're getting numbers no one
has ever seen?"

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:23.029
"Eleventeen, pleventeen.

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:26.832
Something called a thricks.

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:31.137
That's the first thrick
we've ever seen, you guys."

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.038
We know Trump is lying
because polls

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:36.075
have consistently shown that
about half of Americans

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.176
want him at least impeached

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:39.145
if not removed
from office altogether.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:42.415
Even a new Fox News poll
over the weekend confirmed that.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.783
And it was a poll that surprised

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.751
even "Fox &amp; Friends"
morning host

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.219
Brian Kilmeade, who said
this morning

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:50.055
that he was stunned to see
how high the number was.

00:04:50.055 --> 00:04:54.827
-In the latest Fox News poll,
50% of registered voters

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.996
think the President
should be impeached

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:58.898
and removed from office,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:01.400
up one point since October.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.569
Four percent think he should
be impeached

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.838
but not removed from office.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:09.742
And 41% do not think
he should be impeached at all.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.610
-The Fox poll came out.
And I was stunned by this.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.280
It says 50% of the country
want the president impeached.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.948
I was stunned to see that
that's the number

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:18.984
because I thought things
were trending away.

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:20.152
-You know why you thought that?

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:21.521
Because you only
listen to Trump.

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:23.122
And you only watch Fox News.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:26.892
You're like a guy who works at
Arby's who eats an actual burger

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.227
for the first time and says,
"What?

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.562
This burger
doesn't taste like horse."

00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:33.466
[ Laughter ]
When Kilmeade saw that poll,

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:35.468
he was probably like,
"But I thought Trump's approval

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:39.104
rating was up
to eleventeen thricks.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:41.274
That's what I heard."

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:42.742
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:45.411
So Trump is clearly both been
watching impeachment coverage

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.879
and also getting
enraged about it.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:48.847
Although he'd love for us
to believe he's not.

00:05:48.847 --> 00:05:50.916
On Friday, for example,
he insisted he was working

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:54.187
on other, more important issues,
like a supposed trade deal

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.288
he keeps claiming
he's negotiating with China.

00:05:56.288 --> 00:05:58.224
-Mr. President, your reaction
to the votes in the House

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:00.159
Judiciary this morning?

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:04.063
-Well, I was actually, believe
it or not, finishing up the --

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.565
I was doing the final touches
on the China deal.

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:08.367
-I do not believe it.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.002
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:15.474
Also, if you do anything,
it's not the final touches.

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:17.242
They maybe let you help out
in the beginning

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:18.810
a little bit
so you have ownership.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:21.347
You know, the way you let
your toddler stir the frosting

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:24.850
but not put the cake
in the oven.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:26.785
So now that impeachment
is almost certain to pass

00:06:26.785 --> 00:06:28.754
in the House, it will move
to the Senate for trial,

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:32.124
where the Senators themselves
will act as jurors.

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:34.894
And Republican Senators,
who will act as those jurors,

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:36.595
are already on TV
defending the President

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:38.097
before the trial even begins.

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:40.967
For example, there was Senator
Rand Paul, who kept insisting

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:43.102
in a contentious interview
with CNN's Jake Tapper

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:46.038
that Trump was just worried
about corruption in general,

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:47.940
even though several of Trump's
closest associates

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.408
have been arrested and jailed.

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:51.877
And Paul just kept mindlessly
repeating his talking points.

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:55.080
-All of them have been convicted
of federal crimes.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.383
You really think President Trump
is concerned

00:06:57.383 --> 00:07:00.452
about rooting out corruption?

00:07:00.452 --> 00:07:01.920
-I think most of what you
listed,

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.056
and most of the people
that were indicted or convicted,

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:07.860
were alleged to have been some
sort of huge Russian conspiracy.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.395
-I'm asking about President
Trump and corruption.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:12.097
I just listed a number of close
associates of President Trump's

00:07:12.097 --> 00:07:13.732
who are either in prison or --
-Right.

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:15.234
But I think it's based
on opinion.

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:18.137
It's based on opinion
on foreign aids.

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:19.772
-These are criminal convictions.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:22.307
I just wanted to know,
do you really think

00:07:22.307 --> 00:07:24.710
President Trump
is concerned about corruption?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.811
Just a yes or no.

00:07:25.811 --> 00:07:26.745
Is that something
you really believe?

00:07:26.745 --> 00:07:27.980
-Yes, I do think --

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.316
I do think that Ukraine --
I think Ukraine has been

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:32.284
one of the corruptest countries
on Earth.

00:07:32.284 --> 00:07:34.386
-That's not what I asked.

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.555
-All the governments of Ukraine
have been corrupt.

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:38.190
-He kept ignoring the question.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.826
There's no way to break through
with these guys.

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:43.095
They just recite
their preprogrammed lines.

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:45.698
Anchors have to yell at them
the way you yell

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:48.467
at one of those automated
customer service agents.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:49.801
Hello?

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:52.605
-Thank you for calling Verizon.
How can I help you?

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:54.640
-Yeah, I want
to cancel my service.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.176
-I heard "I want
to upgrade my service."

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:58.644
Is that correct?
-No!

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.279
No, no, I said I want to cancel!

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:04.082
-I heard "please add a second
phone line to my account."

00:08:04.082 --> 00:08:07.352
Is that correct?
-No, I want to cancel!

00:08:07.352 --> 00:08:09.688
-I heard "I love Verizon."

00:08:09.688 --> 00:08:11.524
Thank you. Goodbye.

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:13.593
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:19.297
-The argument --
the argument that Trump

00:08:19.297 --> 00:08:21.434
was just concerned
about corruption in general

00:08:21.434 --> 00:08:23.435
is obviously absurd on its face.

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:26.539
In fact, as we speak,
Trump's lawyer, Rudy Giuliani,

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:28.474
who's at the center of this
whole scheme,

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:30.142
is back in the U.S.

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:33.346
from a trip to Ukraine where he
was still digging up dirt

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:34.680
on Trump's political rivals.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.549
And "The Wall Street Journal"
reports that Rudy

00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:38.985
is still reporting
directly to Trump.

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:40.486
When he returned to New York
last Saturday,

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.120
the President called him
as his plane

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.923
was still taxiing down
the runway.

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:45.324
"What did you get?"
Trump asked.

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:47.860
"More than you can imagine,"
Giuliani replied.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.596
He was loudly committing crimes
on the plane

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:51.997
as soon as the plane landed.

00:08:51.997 --> 00:08:54.967
At this point, whenever Rudy
flies, the flight attendants

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:57.770
are going to have to announce
his Miranda rights.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.038
"You are now free
to use your mobile devices.

00:09:00.038 --> 00:09:01.774
And remember,
anything you say can

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:04.710
and will be used against you
in a court of law."

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.913
Not only are they continuing to
cheat the election as we speak,

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:10.949
but they're also trying to cheat
in the trial about the cheating.

00:09:10.949 --> 00:09:13.652
Remember, the Senate is supposed
to be a fair and impartial jury.

00:09:13.652 --> 00:09:14.853
But both Senate majority leader

00:09:14.853 --> 00:09:17.122
Mitch McConnell and Senate
Judiciary chairman

00:09:17.122 --> 00:09:20.459
Lindsay Graham have said
explicitly their only goal

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:22.394
is to end the trial
as quickly as possible,

00:09:22.394 --> 00:09:24.664
call zero witnesses,
and take their marching orders

00:09:24.664 --> 00:09:26.365
directly from
the President himself.

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:29.402
-I don't need
any witnesses at all.

00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:32.405
-Okay, and then --
-I am ready to go.

00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:34.606
My goal is to end this
as soon as possible

00:09:34.606 --> 00:09:37.175
for the good of the country.
-I wasn't -- at this point.

00:09:37.175 --> 00:09:39.478
-I'm not trying to pretend
to be a fair juror here.

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:41.346
-Everything I do during this,

00:09:41.346 --> 00:09:43.115
I'm coordinating
with White House counsel.

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:45.817
There will be no difference
between the President's position

00:09:45.817 --> 00:09:50.255
and our position
as to how to handle this.

00:09:50.255 --> 00:09:51.623
-They're supposed to be
the jury,

00:09:51.623 --> 00:09:52.958
and they're literally
going on TV

00:09:52.958 --> 00:09:55.027
admitting they're not
going to be impartial.

00:09:55.027 --> 00:09:57.096
And they're going to take
their orders from the President.

00:09:57.096 --> 00:10:00.032
Only in the Senate
can you openly brag

00:10:00.032 --> 00:10:01.834
that you're not pretending
to be a fair jury.

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:04.570
Lindsey Graham sounds like a
dude who's just making stuff up

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:06.171
to get out of jury duty.

00:10:06.171 --> 00:10:07.572
"I can't serve on a jury.

00:10:07.572 --> 00:10:09.641
My grandma's sick,
and I'm her caretaker,

00:10:09.641 --> 00:10:11.610
and I'm cat sitting,
and I live far away,

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:14.112
and I don't speak English,
and I'm biased against cops."

00:10:14.112 --> 00:10:15.914
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:15.914 --> 00:10:19.384
This is the Republican Party
of Trump,

00:10:19.384 --> 00:10:23.288
a party that sees any challenge
to its power as illegitimate,

00:10:23.288 --> 00:10:25.057
that's fine with cheating
to win elections

00:10:25.057 --> 00:10:27.960
and that rigs trials to avoid
consequences for that cheating.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.729
They don't care
what they have to do to win,

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:31.163
even if it involves cheating

00:10:31.163 --> 00:10:33.899
and then defending that cheating
by going on TV and spouting --

00:10:33.899 --> 00:10:35.100
-Bull[bleep].

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.136
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:37.136 --> 00:10:38.771
[ Cheers and applause ]

